docker compose restart service - only stops and re-starts an existing container process without applying configuration or image updates


docker compose up -d --build --force-recreate service -  forces Docker to recompile the Dockerfile, destroy the old container, and build a brand-new one from scratch

docker compose up -d --build <service_name>
-  You must rebuild so Docker can run npm install or pip install again inside the image pipeline. 
 -  Note: You do not need the --force-recreate flag here; --build is smart enough to replace the container automatically when the image changes

